931</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id> <sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1054496A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </nplcit> </non-patent-citations> </citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOIKE KUNIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA HIDENORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEIKO EPSON CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU EISAKU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOIKE, KUNIO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, HIDENORI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEIKO EPSON CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU, EISAKU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOIKE KUNIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA HIDENORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU EISAKU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOIKE, KUNIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, HIDENORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU, EISAKU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An electronic device comprises a generator (20) as a power supply, a capacitor (30) for storing generated electric power, a logic circuit (170) driven by the electric power from the capacitor, and a power switch circuit (31). The circuit (31) interrupts the supply to the logic circuit (170) until the voltage of capacitor (30) supplied by the generator reaches a set voltage and then allows the capacitor to energize the logic circuit when the set voltage is exceeded. Since initial leakage current is prevented and substantially the whole power generated is stored in the capacitor, the capacitor can be charged in a shorter time so that an electronic circuit driven by the capacitor can be quickly started.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un dispositif électronique comportant un générateur (20) comme bloc d'alimentation, un condensateur (30) pour stocker l'énergie électrique produite, un circuit logique (170) alimenté par l'énergie électrique provenant du condensateur, et un circuit interrupteur d'alimentation (31). Le circuit (31) coupe l'alimentation en direction du circuit logique (170) tant que la tension du condensateur (30) fournie par le générateur n'atteint pas une tension de consigne, et laisse ensuite le condensateur alimenter le circuit logique lorsque la tension de consigne est dépassée. Comme tout courant de fuite initial est empêché et que pratiquement toute la puissance produite est stockée dans le condensateur, le condensateur peut être chargé en un temps plus court, ce qui permet de faire démarrer rapidement un circuit électronique alimenté par le condensateur.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>